<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Estanislao López</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1786–1838</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Estanislao López was governor of Santa Fe in the Argentine Littoral from 1818 until his death and one of the leading Federalist caudillos. An ally of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-gervasio-artigas">José Gervasio Artigas</a> in the Federal League, he made peace with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-pilar">Treaty of Pilar</a> in 1820, then fought his former partner <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francisco-ramirez">Francisco Ramírez</a>, whose head he displayed in Santa Fe in 1821. In 1831 his men captured the Unitarian general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-maria-paz">José María Paz</a>, breaking the Unitarian League.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/estanislao-lopez.jpg" alt="Estanislao López" width="320" height="436" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Charles Pellegrini · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Estanislao_L%C3%B3pez.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
